// OPTIONAL — README "Photo privacy", option A. Only for a gateway whose agent on PandaBase's
// channels uses a cloud reply model; the `pandabase` agent on a local model (option C) doesn't need
// it. The owner decides; nothing applies this automatically.
//
// The agent bound to #pandabase (and its cycle threads) gets a model that OpenClaw treats as
// text-only, so a photo whose local description failed is never attached to a cloud request:
// OpenClaw injects images only into turns whose model is marked image-capable. The PandaBase
// skills never need pixels (the local Ollama description is enough).
//
// The text-only model is your usual cloud model registered a second time under its own provider
// id with `input: ["text"]`, so other agents on the gateway keep vision. Shown for Anthropic; for
// another vendor use its `api` adapter and base URL (OpenClaw docs: gateway/config-tools/custom-providers).
//
// Apply the provider below like openclaw.pandabase.example.json5 (copy to
// agent/openclaw.privacy.json5, fill the <…>, `openclaw config patch --file … --dry-run`, then for
// real). Then point the agent bound to #pandabase at it by index, not by patch: `agents.list` and
// `bindings` are arrays shared with the gateway's other agents, and a patch would replace them.
//
//   openclaw config get agents.list --json        # find the agent bound to #pandabase
//   openclaw config set "agents.list[<i>].model" '"pandabase-text/<MODEL_ID>"' --strict-json
//
// If no agent is bound to #pandabase yet, add one to `agents.list` by hand (keep the others), e.g.
//   { id: "pandabase", workspace: "~/.openclaw/workspace-pandabase",
//     model: "pandabase-text/<MODEL_ID>", tools: { deny: ["group:web", "browser"] } }
// and a binding for the channel to `bindings` (keep the other agents' channel and DM bindings):
//   { agentId: "pandabase", match: { channel: "discord", guildId: "<GUILD_ID>",
//     peer: { kind: "channel", id: "<PANDABASE_CHANNEL_ID>" } } }
// then set OPENCLAW_AGENT=pandabase in .env and re-run `make install-agent-cron`.
{
  models: {
    providers: {
      "pandabase-text": {
        baseUrl: "https://api.anthropic.com",
        api: "anthropic-messages",
        apiKey: "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}",
        models: [{ id: "<MODEL_ID>", name: "<MODEL_ID> (text only)", input: ["text"] }],
      },
    },
  },
}
